--
The parameters of a requires-expression were parsed as a type-id followed
by an optional name.  `int (&a)[5]' did not parse, so the list was
skipped, and `int (*fp)(int)' parsed as an unnamed `int (*)(int)'; either
way the names were unknown in the requirements, which then failed.
